fix: stop exposing sensitive profile fields (H1 / P0-3)

Any authenticated user could read every profile's email via the
"Profiles are viewable by everyone" policy. profiles keeps its row-level
select policy because chat legitimately needs cross-user display
names/avatars, so the sensitive data is removed at the column level:

- Drop the email column entirely (auth.users is the source of truth; the
  app shows user.email from the session). With no column there is nothing
  to enumerate. admin_list_users is recreated to read email from
  auth.users, still gated behind is_server_admin().
- Revoke SELECT (server_admin) from authenticated. Admin gating moves to
  the existing is_server_admin() RPC via a new useIsServerAdmin hook.
  AuthContext fetches explicit columns (no server_admin).

Client:
- useIsServerAdmin hook (loading-aware).
- App nav, AdminView, Lobby, CreateChannelModal use the hook instead of
  profile.server_admin.
- ProfileSettings shows user.email instead of profile.email.
- database.ts: drop email from the profiles type; add is_server_admin RPC.
